    "ss_home_faq_giy86J": {
      "type": "ss-home-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_j68aBc": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much data comes with the Malaysia eSIM starting at $0.91?",
            "answer": "The Malaysia eSIM offers several prepaid data allowances, so you can choose an option based on how long you are there and how you intend to use your phone. Available packages include 100MB, 500MB, 1GB, 3GB, 5GB, 10GB, 20GB, and 50GB. Validity varies by package, with options suited to short visits and longer trips. The lowest advertised starting price may change, so check the current price displayed on the product page before purchasing. eSIMnow’s Malaysia plan provides full-speed data rather than reducing your connection speed after a daily allowance. Consider how much data you need for navigation, messaging, browsing, and video streaming before selecting your package."
          }
        },
        "question_bQJB69": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long is the Malaysia eSIM data plan valid for?",
            "answer": "The validity period depends on the Malaysia data package you select. Current options include 100MB, 500MB, and 1GB plans valid for 7 days; a 3GB plan valid for either 15 or 30 days; and 5GB, 10GB, and 20GB plans valid for 30 days. A 50GB option is also listed with 30-day or 180-day validity. This range gives you flexibility for a brief visit, a longer holiday, or an extended stay. Before buying, match the validity period to your travel dates and check the selected package details carefully. The eSIM has a 180-day pre-activation window, which allows you to purchase it in advance of your trip."
          }
        },
        "question_BaANgt": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I top up my Malaysia eSIM once the data runs out?",
            "answer": "Yes. The Malaysia eSIM supports top-ups, so you can add more data if your original allowance runs low during your trip. This can be convenient if you use more mobile internet than expected for maps, messaging, online searches, or sharing photos. You may be able to continue using your existing eSIM instead of installing a completely new one. Top-up availability does not mean that extra data is added automatically, so check your eSIMnow order details and follow the available top-up instructions when needed. It is also worth monitoring your data consumption throughout your stay. If you expect heavy usage, choosing a larger package at the outset may be more convenient."
          }
        },
        "question_RVKMRA": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does this eSIM support calls and SMS in Malaysia?",
            "answer": "The Malaysia eSIM is a data-only plan. It doesn't come with a local mobile number for traditional cellular calls or SMS messages. You can, however, use its mobile data connection with internet-based communication services, including messaging and voice or video calling apps. This lets you contact friends, family, or colleagues while traveling, provided you have the relevant apps and an internet connection. If you need to receive standard text messages, make ordinary cellular calls, or use a number for local services, check whether your existing SIM can remain active for those functions. With eSIMnow, the Malaysia plan handles mobile data separately, so review your phone’s SIM settings before departure."
          }
        },
        "question_he3y6z": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will I be charged roaming fees using this eSIM in Malaysia?",
            "answer": "The Malaysia eSIM is a prepaid travel data plan advertised without hidden roaming fees when used within its supported coverage. You select and pay for your data package before relying on the connection, helping you avoid unexpected data-roaming charges from your usual mobile carrier. To reduce the risk of charges from your primary SIM, check your phone’s mobile data settings and select the Malaysia eSIM for data use. You may also want to turn off data roaming on your regular SIM while traveling. Keep in mind that charges from your existing carrier can still depend on its own settings and services, so review its roaming terms separately before departure."
          }
        },
        "question_8xNmr6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which networks does the Malaysia eSIM connect to?",
            "answer": "The eSIMnow Malaysia eSIM lists Maxis 5G and CelcomDigi 5G as its supported local networks. These networks provide the connection used by the eSIM to access mobile data in Malaysia. Your actual experience can vary depending on where you are, the coverage available in that area, your phone’s capabilities, and the local network. A 5G network listing does not guarantee that your device will always connect at 5G speeds, since coverage and compatibility affect the connection. Before traveling, check that your phone supports eSIM technology and the relevant mobile network bands. The plan is designed for use in Malaysia, so do not assume it includes service in neighboring countries."
          }
        },
        "question_JmJyWQ": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How soon should I activate the eSIM before arriving in Malaysia?",
            "answer": "You can purchase the Malaysia eSIM ahead of your trip because eSIMnow lists a 180-day pre-activation window. This means you do not need to wait until the last moment to buy and prepare your plan. The product instructions say the eSIM can start upon arrival, when it connects to a supported local network. Follow the installation instructions provided with your purchase, and check the activation guidance before traveling so you know which steps to complete in advance and which to leave until arrival. Keep your QR code and installation details accessible. Avoid deleting the eSIM profile once installed unless eSIMnow’s instructions or support team advises you to do so."
          }
        },
        "question_TdxrxN": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use this eSIM for hotspot or tethering?",
            "answer": "Yes. The Malaysia eSIM lists hotspot functionality as supported, making it possible for you to share your phone’s mobile data connection with compatible devices such as a laptop or tablet. This can be useful when you need internet access for work, travel planning, or other tasks on a second device. To use it, enable the hotspot or tethering feature in your phone’s settings and connect your other device as you normally would. Remember that connected devices use data from your Malaysia eSIM package, so activities such as video calls, large downloads, and streaming can consume your allowance quickly. Check your phone’s hotspot settings and keep track of your remaining data during your trip."
          }
        },
        "question_pMRLQy": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is my phone eSIM-compatible for use in Malaysia?",
            "answer": "Your device should be able to handle eSIM technology to use the Malaysia eSIM, and it generally needs to be carrier-unlocked. Compatibility depends on the exact model and, in some cases, the region where the device was sold. Many newer iPhone and Android models support eSIM, but it is best not to rely on the brand name alone. Before purchasing, use the Device Compatibility checker linked on eSIMnow’s Malaysia product page to check your specific device. You should also confirm that your phone can install an additional eSIM profile and that you can access its mobile network settings. Checking compatibility before departure helps reduce the chance of connection problems during your trip."
          }
        }
      },
